<title>TURKEY: Turk Cukurova Elektrik pays out dividend.</title>
<headline>Turk Cukurova Elektrik pays out dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's biggest private sector utility Cukurova Elektrik said it began paying out a dividend 9,676.5 lira per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from Tuesday.</p>
<p>In a statement sent to the Istanbul Stock Exchange, the company said distribution of dividends from 1996 profits was approved at the company's annual meeting of shareholders and directors on Monday.</p>
<p>Cukurova had reported 5.45 trillion lira of net profits in 1996, up sharply from 538.41 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
